    "custom_liquid_xrNF6E": {
      "type": "custom-liquid",
      "name": "Custom Liquid",
      "settings": {
        "use_container": true,
        "custom_liquid": "<h2 style=\"weight: 600;width: 100%; text-align: center; margin-bottom: 8px; font-size: 1.8rem; padding: 20px 0;font-size:24px;\">Malpelo Foundation Alliance</h2>\n\n<div style=\"position: relative; width: 100%; padding-bottom: 56.25%; height: 0;\">\n  <iframe \n      src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/xnTkt1Askzg\"\n      style=\"position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%;\"\n      frameborder=\"0\"\n      allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture\"\n      allowfullscreen>\n  </iframe>\n</div>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 20px;margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 20px;line-height: 1.7;color:#001c39;\">Sutex in alliance with Leonisa and the Malpelo Foundation, we carried out a campaign in favor of marine ecosystems. A strategy with the aim of transforming the situation of sharks in the Colombian Pacific. For this campaign, Sutex and Leonisa developed a collection of printed face masks that were put on sale nationwide.</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 20px;margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 20px;line-height: 1.7;color:#001c39;\">100% of the money raised would go to the Malpelo Foundation, to finance expeditions in which sharks are tagged with satellite and acoustic telemetry, monitoring their movements and identifying breeding areas. Likewise, to support research, shark protection and care of marine and coastal areas in Colombia and the world.</p>"
      }
    },
    "custom_liquid_q3YLaF": {
      "type": "custom-liquid",
      "name": "Custom Liquid",
      "settings": {
        "use_container": true,
        "custom_liquid": "<h2 style=\"width: 100%; text-align: center; margin-bottom: 30px; font-size: 1.8rem; border-bottom: 2px solid #001c39; padding: 20px 0;font-weight: 600;\">Recycling Plant</h2>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 20px;margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 20px;line-height: 1.7;color:#001c39;\">We opened our first plastic processing plant. Thanks to this, we are transforming the caps of PET plastic bottles into elements for internal use for the company, such as hooks, pots, key rings, among other products.</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-top: 20px;margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 20px;line-height: 1.7;color:#001c39;\">At Sutex we want our employees to continue to appropriate the culture of reduce, recycle and reuse. We instill in them the love for the planet and the importance of small daily actions from the development of their functions and the use of resources, without generating unnecessary waste.</p>"
      }
    },
